[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [{:db/id 17592186198370 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-216ab53f-9c7f-5387-ad09-67452d907209"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-216ab53f-9c7f-5387-ad09-67452d907209" :question/id #uuid "216ab53f-9c7f-5387-ad09-67452d907209" :question/math-academy-id "q-160572" :question/problem "Consider all non-critical points of the transformation $T:(u,v)\\to (x(u,v),y(u,v)).$ The inverse transformation ${T}^{-1}(x,y)\\to (u(x,y),v(x,y))$ is given by\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}xy \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{y}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFind the Jacobian determinant of $T$ in terms of $u$ and $v.$" :question/worked-solution "Given a transformation \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, we're only given ${T}^{-1}.$ So, we compute the Jacobian determinant of $T$ as follows:\n\n- First, we compute $\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)},$ the Jacobian determinant of ${T}^{-1}.$\n\n- Then, we will compute the Jacobian determinant of $T$ using the relation\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}={(\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)})}^{-1}.\n$$\n\nHere, we have $u(x,y)=xy$ and $v(x,y)=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{y}.$ \n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & =y & \\,\\frac{∂u}{∂y} & =x \\\\ \\frac{∂v}{∂x} & =\\frac{2x}{y} & \\,\\frac{∂v}{∂y} & =-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & \\frac{∂u}{∂y} \\\\ \\frac{∂v}{∂x} & \\frac{∂v}{∂y}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}y & x \\\\ \\frac{2x}{y} & -\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =y\\cdot (-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}})-x\\cdot \\frac{2x}{y} \\\\  & =\\frac{-3{x}^{2}}{y} \\\\  & =-3\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{2}}{y} \\\\  & =-3v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we take the reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & ={(\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)})}^{-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3v}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3aa3cd04-7b64-5645-9bfe-bb149f8d1b73"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3aa3cd04-7b64-5645-9bfe-bb149f8d1b73" :answer-field/id #uuid "3aa3cd04-7b64-5645-9bfe-bb149f8d1b73" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c4ff2ce6-b380-5ab9-9fa2-41399e5c2bf3" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c4ff2ce6-b380-5ab9-9fa2-41399e5c2bf3" "answer-a0e1f31b-7a73-5f60-aa37-ebb1960532b8" "answer-1da512ca-3f7f-55fa-ba92-0e0c6f6c21be" "answer-cabf98b2-4e8b-519a-86a9-7f344c20fcb7" "answer-3f9f7694-d0a1-5a9c-8f7b-8ada526129f3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c4ff2ce6-b380-5ab9-9fa2-41399e5c2bf3" :answer/id #uuid "c4ff2ce6-b380-5ab9-9fa2-41399e5c2bf3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3v}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a0e1f31b-7a73-5f60-aa37-ebb1960532b8" :answer/id #uuid "a0e1f31b-7a73-5f60-aa37-ebb1960532b8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{v}{u}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1da512ca-3f7f-55fa-ba92-0e0c6f6c21be" :answer/id #uuid "1da512ca-3f7f-55fa-ba92-0e0c6f6c21be" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-v" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cabf98b2-4e8b-519a-86a9-7f344c20fcb7" :answer/id #uuid "cabf98b2-4e8b-519a-86a9-7f344c20fcb7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3v" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3f9f7694-d0a1-5a9c-8f7b-8ada526129f3" :answer/id #uuid "3f9f7694-d0a1-5a9c-8f7b-8ada526129f3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :an